{"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SwiftWorkflow"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Deploying and Persisting Scientific Workflows"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftWorkflow\/documentation\/SwiftWorkflow"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftworkflow\/workflowpersistence"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftWorkflow\/documentation\/SwiftWorkflow\/WorkflowPersistence"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to safely persist, reload, and evaluate end-to-end machine learning workflows across processes."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In production scientific machine learning systems, data leakage between training and evaluation phases is one of the most common causes of overly optimistic validation metrics. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftWorkflow"},{"type":"text","text":" eliminates leakage by enforcing structural invariants at the API level:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit Supervised Batch Splitting"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Workflows accept "},{"code":"PreparedSupervisedBatch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instances where row selection explicitly tracks "},{"code":"originalRowIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Immutable Stages"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Once trained, a workflow exposes no mutable hyperparameters or refitting paths."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Atomic Schema Validation"}]},{"type":"text","text":": When loading from JSON, dimensions and feature names are checked against the artifact header before initializing models."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"End-to-End-Persistence-Pattern","type":"heading","text":"End-to-End Persistence Pattern"},{"code":["import Foundation","import SwiftDataFrame","import SwiftWorkflow","","\/\/ Train workflow on designated training rows","let workflow = try await PCAClassificationWorkflow.train(","    training: trainingBatch,","    components: 2,","    learningRate: 0.125,","    epochs: 64",")","","\/\/ Serialize fitted stages to JSON artifact","let artifactURL = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"PCAWorkflow.json\")","try workflow.save(to: artifactURL)","","\/\/ Reload across independent processes with verified dimensions","let reloaded = try PCAClassificationWorkflow.load(from: artifactURL)","let predictions = try await reloaded.predict(unlabeledBatch)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftWorkflow/documentation/SwiftWorkflow":{"title":"SwiftWorkflow","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiftworkflow","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftWorkflow\/documentation\/SwiftWorkflow","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Production Machine Learning Pipelines, Preprocessing Composition, and Artifact Serialization."}]}}}